<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13414] JDBC thin: compatibility is broken for versions 2.8-2.9</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13414</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&quot;User attributes&quot; feature was added by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12049&quot; title=&quot;Add user attributes to thin clients&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-12049&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-12049&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, it was added to 2.9 version, but for VER_2_8_0 condition:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
         &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (ver.compareTo(VER_2_8_0) &amp;gt;= 0) {
            dataPageScanEnabled = nullableBooleanFromByte(reader.readByte());

            updateBatchSize = JdbcUtils.readNullableInteger(reader);

            userAttrs = reader.readMap();
        }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This breaks compatibility between 2.8 and 2.9 versions (both, backward and forward)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
